data: {"delta":"Based on the evidence, here's the current Node.js version status:\n\n**Latest LTS Version: Node.js 26**\n- Version: 26.13.0 (Lithium)\n- Release Date: October 29, 2026\n- Status: Entered LTS on October 29, 2026 [5]\n\n**Current Version Line:**\n- Node.js 26 is now the Current version line [5]\n- The next version (Node.js 27) is expected to follow the new release schedule of one major version per year [5]\n\n**Previous Status:**\n- Node.js 24 left Active LTS on October 20, 2026 [4]\n\nStarting with Node.js 27, the project is changing to one major release per year, with each version reaching LTS after spending half a year as Current [5].","conversationId":"cmw01t00y0004qa9admokkr57"}

